S:alignment: data/raw_data/swaralipi/rs001363.pdf (Geetabitan swaralipi)
N:Notes quantized to 16ths, pitch bends applied (scripts/midi_to_ktab.py read_tracks). Sa = C; Ma is mostly tivra (F#), shuddha Ma (F) in "horini" and the refrain.
N:Form played by the MIDI: sthayi; antara (its first two lines twice) and the refrain "Maayabono biharini"; sanchari (its first line twice); abhog (its first two lines twice) and the refrain.
N:Long compound words of the lyrics file are split into words for the tab (Maa-ya-bo-no bi-ha-ri-ni, Ga-ho-no swa-po-no san-cha-ri-ni). "Parosho kori or" follows the swaralipi: pa-ro-sho ko-ri-bo or.
N:Syllables placed on the notes as in the swaralipi; one swaralipi matra = one quarter note, one half-bar of 4 matras = one 4/4 bar.
